#: ../../../userspace-api/liveupdate.rst:9
msgid "ioctl interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/liveupdate:10: ../kernel/liveupdate/luo_core.c:250
msgid ""
"The IOCTL user-space control interface for the LUO subsystem. It registers a "
"character device, typically found at ``/dev/liveupdate``, which allows a "
"userspace agent to manage the LUO state machine and its associated "
"resources, such as preservable file descriptors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/liveupdate:10: ../kernel/liveupdate/luo_core.c:255
msgid ""
"To ensure that the state machine is controlled by a single entity, access to "
"this device is exclusive: only one process is permitted to have ``/dev/"
"liveupdate`` open at any given time. Subsequent open attempts will fail with "
"-EBUSY until the first process closes its file descriptor. This singleton "
"model simplifies state management by preventing conflicting commands from "
"multiple userspace agents."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/liveupdate.rst:14
msgid "ioctl uAPI"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/liveupdate:15: ../include/uapi/linux/liveupdate.h:3
msgid "**General ioctl format**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/liveupdate:15: ../include/uapi/linux/liveupdate.h:18
msgid ""
"The ioctl interface follows a general format to allow for extensibility. "
"Each ioctl is passed in a structure pointer as the argument providing the "
"size of the structure in the first u32. The kernel checks that any structure "
"space beyond what it understands is 0. This allows userspace to use the "
"backward compatible portion while consistently using the newer, larger, "
"structures."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/liveupdate:15: ../include/uapi/linux/liveupdate.h:24
msgid "ioctls use a standard meaning for common errnos:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/liveupdate:15: ../include/uapi/linux/liveupdate.h:26
msgid "ENOTTY: The IOCTL number itself is not supported at all"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/liveupdate:15: ../include/uapi/linux/liveupdate.h:27
msgid ""
"E2BIG: The IOCTL number is supported, but the provided structure has non-"
"zero in a part the kernel does not understand."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/liveupdate:15: ../include/uapi/linux/liveupdate.h:29
msgid ""
"EOPNOTSUPP: The IOCTL number is supported, and the structure is understood, "
"however a known field has a value the kernel does not understand or support."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/liveupdate:15: ../include/uapi/linux/liveupdate.h:32
msgid ""
"EINVAL: Everything about the IOCTL was understood, but a field is not "
"correct."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/liveupdate:15: ../include/uapi/linux/liveupdate.h:34
msgid "ENOENT: A provided token does not exist."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/liveupdate:15: ../include/uapi/linux/liveupdate.h:35
msgid "ENOMEM: Out of memory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/liveupdate:15: ../include/uapi/linux/liveupdate.h:36
msgid "EOVERFLOW: Mathematics overflowed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/liveupdate:15: ../include/uapi/linux/liveupdate.h:38
msgid "As well as additional errnos, within specific ioctls."
msgstr ""

