#: ../../../userspace-api/liveupdate:15: ../include/uapi/linux/liveupdate.h:88
msgid "ioctl(LIVEUPDATE_IOCTL_RETRIEVE_SESSION)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/liveupdate:15: ../include/uapi/linux/liveupdate.h:90
msgid "Input; sizeof(struct liveupdate_ioctl_retrieve_session)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/liveupdate:15: ../include/uapi/linux/liveupdate.h:91
msgid "Output; The new file descriptor for the retrieved session."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/liveupdate:15: ../include/uapi/linux/liveupdate.h:92
msgid ""
"Input; A null-terminated string identifying the session to retrieve. The "
"name must exactly match the name used when the session was created in the "
"previous kernel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/liveupdate:15: ../include/uapi/linux/liveupdate.h:94
msgid ""
"Retrieves a handle (a new file descriptor) for a preserved session by its "
"name. This is the primary mechanism for a userspace agent to regain control "
"of its preserved resources after a live update."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/liveupdate:15: ../include/uapi/linux/liveupdate.h:98
msgid ""
"The userspace application provides the null-terminated `name` of a session "
"it created before the live update. If a preserved session with a matching "
"name is found, the kernel instantiates it and returns a new file descriptor "
"in the `fd` field. This new session FD can then be used for all file-"
"specific operations, such as restoring individual file descriptors with "
"LIVEUPDATE_SESSION_RETRIEVE_FD."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/liveupdate:15: ../include/uapi/linux/liveupdate.h:105
msgid ""
"It is the responsibility of the userspace application to know the names of "
"the sessions it needs to retrieve. If no session with the given name is "
"found, the ioctl will fail with -ENOENT."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/liveupdate:15: ../include/uapi/linux/liveupdate.h:109
msgid ""
"This ioctl can only be called on the main /dev/liveupdate device when the "
"system is in the LIVEUPDATE_STATE_UPDATED state."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/liveupdate:15: ../include/uapi/linux/liveupdate.h:125
msgid "ioctl(LIVEUPDATE_SESSION_PRESERVE_FD)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/liveupdate:15: ../include/uapi/linux/liveupdate.h:127
msgid "Input; sizeof(struct liveupdate_session_preserve_fd)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/liveupdate:15: ../include/uapi/linux/liveupdate.h:128
msgid "Input; The user-space file descriptor to be preserved."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/liveupdate:15: ../include/uapi/linux/liveupdate.h:128
#: ../include/uapi/linux/liveupdate.h:162
msgid "``token``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/liveupdate:15: ../include/uapi/linux/liveupdate.h:129
msgid "Input; An opaque, unique token for preserved resource."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/liveupdate:15: ../include/uapi/linux/liveupdate.h:129
msgid "Holds parameters for preserving a file descriptor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/liveupdate:15: ../include/uapi/linux/liveupdate.h:131
msgid ""
"User sets the **fd** field identifying the file descriptor to preserve (e."
"g., memfd, kvm, iommufd, VFIO). The kernel validates if this FD type and its "
"dependencies are supported for preservation. If validation passes, the "
"kernel marks the FD internally and *initiates the process* of preparing its "
"state for saving. The actual snapshotting of the state typically occurs "
"during the subsequent ``LIVEUPDATE_IOCTL_PREPARE`` execution phase, though "
"some finalization might occur during freeze. On successful validation and "
"initiation, the kernel uses the **token** field with an opaque identifier "
"representing the resource being preserved. This token confirms the FD is "
"targeted for preservation and is required for the subsequent "
"``LIVEUPDATE_SESSION_RETRIEVE_FD`` call after the live update."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/liveupdate:15: ../include/uapi/linux/liveupdate.h:144
msgid ""
"0 on success (validation passed, preservation initiated), negative error "
"code on failure (e.g., unsupported FD type, dependency issue, validation "
"failed)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/liveupdate:15: ../include/uapi/linux/liveupdate.h:158
msgid "ioctl(LIVEUPDATE_SESSION_RETRIEVE_FD)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/liveupdate:15: ../include/uapi/linux/liveupdate.h:160
msgid "Input; sizeof(struct liveupdate_session_retrieve_fd)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/liveupdate:15: ../include/uapi/linux/liveupdate.h:161
msgid ""
"Output; The new file descriptor representing the fully restored kernel "
"resource."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/liveupdate:15: ../include/uapi/linux/liveupdate.h:163
msgid "Input; An opaque, token that was used to preserve the resource."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/liveupdate:15: ../include/uapi/linux/liveupdate.h:163
msgid "Retrieve a previously preserved file descriptor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/liveupdate:15: ../include/uapi/linux/liveupdate.h:165
msgid ""
"User sets the **token** field to the value obtained from a successful "
"``LIVEUPDATE_IOCTL_FD_PRESERVE`` call before the live update. On success, "
"the kernel restores the state (saved during the PREPARE/FREEZE phases) "
"associated with the token and populates the **fd** field with a new file "
"descriptor referencing the restored resource in the current (new) kernel. "
"This operation must be performed *before* signaling completion via "
"``LIVEUPDATE_IOCTL_FINISH``. If a retrieve of a token fails, subsequent "
"attempts to retrieve the token fail with the same error code. Failed "
"retrieves are not retried."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/liveupdate:15: ../include/uapi/linux/liveupdate.h:176
msgid "0 on success, negative error code on failure (e.g., invalid token)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/liveupdate:15: ../include/uapi/linux/liveupdate.h:188
msgid "ioctl(LIVEUPDATE_SESSION_FINISH)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/liveupdate:15: ../include/uapi/linux/liveupdate.h:190
msgid "Input; sizeof(struct liveupdate_session_finish)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/liveupdate:15: ../include/uapi/linux/liveupdate.h:190
#: ../include/uapi/linux/liveupdate.h:222
msgid "``reserved``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/liveupdate:15: ../include/uapi/linux/liveupdate.h:191
#: ../include/uapi/linux/liveupdate.h:223
msgid "Input; Must be zero. Reserved for future use."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/liveupdate:15: ../include/uapi/linux/liveupdate.h:191
msgid ""
"Signals the completion of the restoration process for a retrieved session. "
"This is the final operation that should be performed on a session file "
"descriptor after a live update."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/liveupdate:15: ../include/uapi/linux/liveupdate.h:195
msgid ""
"This ioctl must be called once all required file descriptors for the session "
"have been successfully retrieved (using ``LIVEUPDATE_SESSION_RETRIEVE_FD``) "
"and are fully restored from the userspace and kernel perspective."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/liveupdate:15: ../include/uapi/linux/liveupdate.h:199
msgid ""
"Upon success, the kernel releases its ownership of the preserved resources "
"associated with this session. This allows internal resources to be freed, "
"typically by decrementing reference counts on the underlying preserved "
"objects."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/liveupdate:15: ../include/uapi/linux/liveupdate.h:204
msgid ""
"If this operation fails, the resources remain preserved in memory. Userspace "
"may attempt to call finish again. The resources will otherwise be reset "
"during the next live update cycle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/liveupdate:15: ../include/uapi/linux/liveupdate.h:220
msgid "ioctl(LIVEUPDATE_SESSION_GET_NAME)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/liveupdate:15: ../include/uapi/linux/liveupdate.h:222
msgid "Input; sizeof(struct liveupdate_session_get_name)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/liveupdate:15: ../include/uapi/linux/liveupdate.h:224
msgid "Output; A null-terminated string with the full session name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/liveupdate:15: ../include/uapi/linux/liveupdate.h:224
msgid ""
"Retrieves the full name of the session associated with this file descriptor. "
"This is useful because the kernel may truncate the name shown in /proc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/liveupdate.rst:18
msgid "Note on Compatibility"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/liveupdate.rst:20
msgid ""
"Note that the Live Update feature is still under development and subject to "
"change, so compatibility is not guaranteed when kexec rebooting between "
"different kernel versions. This is expected to change and stabilize in a "
"future version."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/liveupdate.rst:26
msgid "Userspace Integration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/liveupdate.rst:28
msgid ""
"systemd (since version v261) uses LUO to preserve its per-service file "
"descriptor store across a kexec-based live update. Services opt in by "
"setting ``FileDescriptorStoreMax=`` and ``FileDescriptorStorePreserve=`` in "
"their unit, and push file descriptors with a name into the store via "
"``sd_pid_notify_with_fds(... \"FDSTORE=1\\nFDNAME=foo\")``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/liveupdate.rst:34
msgid ""
"Services may also create their own LUO sessions (via ``/dev/liveupdate``) "
"and push the resulting session fds into their file descriptor store like any "
"other fd. systemd detects such session fds and handles them accordingly, and "
"hands the re-retrieved session fd back to the service after kexec, using the "
"existing file descriptor store service interface."
msgstr ""

